{
  "reading": "Two cards judged separately on jaws-v1 against the pilot's bar: does it accelerate early pressure on every seat. Torbran: no change -- four screens are flat or worse on killed by T6 and damage @T10; his +2 reaches only red sources, and Shabraz (W/U) is the deck's biggest combat source. Fiery Emancipation: in for Gratuitous Violence -- its oracle text triples ANY source you control (not only red, contrary to the brief), it supersedes Gratuitous Violence's creature-only double at +1 mana, and the goldfish reads killed by T6 and damage @T10 better with no row worse.",
  "log_entries_read": [
    "006"
  ],
  "cut_candidates": [
    {
      "card": "Gratuitous Violence",
      "why": "Fiery Emancipation does its job wider (any source, including spells) and harder (x3 vs x2) for one more mana; the RRR count stays the same.",
      "cost_of_cutting": "One mana: the multiplier lands on T6 instead of T5, at a fast table. It also gives up the cheaper creature-only doubler. Stacks 007, 013 and 014 list it; 013 and 014 also need Razorkin Needlehead, which is not in this list.",
      "difficulty": "contested",
      "orphans_stack": [
        "007",
        "013",
        "014"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "add_candidates": [
    {
      "card": "Fiery Emancipation",
      "closes": "threat-density",
      "source": "prompt",
      "why": "goldfish vs Gratuitous Violence: killed by T6 17.3% -> 18.8% [+1.2, +1.8], damage @T10 172.4 -> 211.5 [+36.1, +42.1], no row worse; it triples Shabraz's commander damage and every red ping.",
      "natural_cut": "Gratuitous Violence"
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Do stacks 007/013 still hold with Gratuitous Violence gone (007 orders three replacements)?",
      "settled_by": "resolve-stack",
      "why_it_matters": "A verified line may lose a piece."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is RRR on curve by T4-T6? The audit's 0.839 lands-only figure uses 2 effective pips, not 3.",
      "settled_by": "goldfish",
      "why_it_matters": "Torbran and Fiery Emancipation are both RRR."
    }
  ],
  "gaps": [
    "try prints no damage @T6/@T8 rows, only killed by T6 and damage @T10.",
    "Damage is measured against one seat; Torbran's +2 on each-opponent pings is undercounted for table-wide life loss.",
    "No blockers and no removal: tripled combat assumes Shabraz connects, and the 6-mana enchantment is never answered."
  ]
}
